sh":"83014259a5ad8fe8f3d2c9769a529c5d05c15cbef49e7407ede2b6904c53cc4d","event_uuid":"ceb55077-abd1-466e-b0ab-44bdcc93617b","position":{"commit_sha":"5858dd6feb93cab4663cefd0336724f9f1fcd03c","position":"1787337794852138936-ceb55077-abd1-466e-b0ab-44bdcc93617b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"24756b9a38cc98dd8c25020495f64f07cd72206e54b614a41a70503c15b35912","event_uuid":"c584acfc-18c0-4d7c-89cd-d64eed020f30","position":{"commit_sha":"ba04dae8deb51c34b2c1a4c47c40ad0520aea17b","position":"1787338676712299001-c584acfc-18c0-4d7c-89cd-d64eed020f30"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"735a3401c0f6a3eac44719ee1d028bfe9b687908093ead92c6ecae126d72a92f","event_uuid":"3fcef354-a0e0-4f64-8362-9d82f218d79d","position":{"commit_sha":"36d1c97f65e79d7f6aaa9cc3ef5285196b9efef7","position":"1787338742668665001-3fcef354-a0e0-4f64-8362-9d82f218d79d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c0aba66ceadce460cfa7aab644df5b32e669685ac5038105ca74a17a52ff434b","event_uuid":"7af96424-ea6c-4bd7-b45c-dd96bc7336f1","position":{"commit_sha":"ed4e0e317d97b48084450af997da165a8b622f62","position":"1787339227362850001-7af96424-ea6c-4bd7-b45c-dd96bc7336f1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"19c39d0b1c525e54aa32b8a7a30784eff42e8bf6b87a366698598a6b5592bd37","event_uuid":"50112193-2bf2-4742-b1a5-fa711a27aefd","position":{"commit_sha":"1e4d98c2a1d65001f84db010065a531b3b7868da","position":"1787339663813732001-50112193-2bf2-4742-b1a5-fa711a27aefd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix implemented in worktree fix-b9b4 (RED→GREEN confirmed).\n\nMECHANISM (verified by RED test): JiraDataCenterBackend.add_comment was a bare delegate to the transport, which hands body straight to the jira client — a 50,000-char decorated body reached the recording client unfitted under a 4,096 ceiling.\n\nCHANGE:\n- DC send path: add_comment now routes through _DCSanitizer.sanitize_comment, whose fit is outbound_comments.fit_preserving_marker over the comment path's own _truncate_dc_comment_body at comment_max_chars() — the exact composition Cloud's send uses (6724e79e8f). Marker-less bodies keep byte-identical behaviour; the operator warning stays in jira_family.sanitize_comment.\n- Dedup-key consistency (the e339/103729e90c class): _DCSanitizer.fit_comment re-derived via fit_comment_as_sent over the same raw fit, so _diff_comments' key equals the marker-stripped landed body. Both sides changed together in one change; convergence pins updated (049e convergence test, DC characterization, DC two-pass convergence suite) to DERIVE expectations from the real send composition.\n- WIRE-vs-REMOVE decision: DC's sanitize_comment WIRED (it is the send-side sanitizer the ticket describes; after the marker-preserving recomposition it matches the needed semantics exactly). Cloud's sanitize_comment REMOVED: Cloud's real send fit is fit_preserving_marker(body, AdfCodec.fit_outbound) inside acli_cli_ops.add_comment (serialized-ADF budget); the dead method's plain 32,767-char cap would cut RECONCILER_MARKER if ever wired — wiring it would reintroduce bug 5931. Removed _JiraSanitizer.sanitize_comment, jira_fields._sanitize_comment, the acli.py facade re-export, and the FieldSanitizer.sanitize_comment protocol member (nothing calls it via the port; DC keeps its concrete wired method).\n\nNew test tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_send_path_comment_fit.py drives the REAL JiraDataCenterTransport + JiraDataCenterBackend with only the jira client stubbed; RED pre-fix on both the length fit and the dedup key, GREEN post-fix; in-limit and ceiling-0 pass-through pinned.\n\nGates: make lint 0, make typecheck 0, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0 (stale=1 = allowed improvement), tests/unit/rebar_reconciler 3010 passed.\n\nUnrelated pre-existing failure found while validating: state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote fails identically on untouched main (git cat-file 128 in a temp bare repo) — not introduced here; will file a discovered_from ticket.","timestamp":1787336868521908001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit change 2013 merged as 46575522d6 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, no unresolved comments). DC send path now fits outbound comments through sanitize_comment -> fit_preserving_marker over comment_max_chars(); fit_comment re-derived via fit_comment_as_sent so the dedup key matches what lands; Cloud's dead sanitize_comment chain removed. Verified post-merge on the rebased tip: 24 targeted tests green alongside concurrent 8209097fa9 (dedup decoder unification).","timestamp":1787338676712299001}],"created_at":1787293635834766001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d694cd84-4cf2-4f6c-8163-909ec6ec06a8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5931-78a3-95d2-44cd"},{"link_uuid":"ceb55077-abd1-466e-b0ab-44bdcc93617b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b393-b974-c869-4602"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFound in the Step 7 parity census for bug `5931-78a3-95d2-44cd`. On Jira Data Center the\noutbound comment send path applies **no length fit at all**, so an over-length comment is\nhanded to Jira unfitted. Bug `6afc-20ee-84e5-4dd5` established Jira exits 0 on an\nover-length rejection, so the comment never lands and is re-emitted every pass — the\noutbound comment-sync loop. DC's ceiling is deployment-resolved (`comment_max_chars()`,\nbug `049e`) and typically low, so an unfitted DC body is MORE likely to be rejected.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/_links.py` `_CommentsMixin.add_comment` passes `body`\n  straight to `self._client.add_comment`; `JiraDataCenterBackend.add_comment` is a bare\n  delegate to it.\n- `_DCSanitizer.sanitize_comment` — the send-side sanitizer with its operator warning —\n  has **no production caller** (grep hits are test files only). The same is true for\n  Cloud's `_JiraSanitizer.sanitize_comment`.\n- `fit_comment` (the differ-side twin) IS wired via `outbound_comments._diff_comments`:\n  the comparison half of the convergence pair is live, the SEND half is not.\n- NOT bug 5931's mechanism (Cloud truncated and lost the marker); DC does not truncate\n  at all — the mirror-image gap.\n\n## Approach\n\n- **Fit the DC send path, reusing the existing marker-preserving fitter — no second\n  fitter.** Wire `_DCSanitizer.sanitize_comment` into `JiraDataCenterBackend.add_comment`\n  (the one production caller of the transport's `add_comment`, covering all three\n  enactment sites), and recompose `sanitize_comment` so its injected `truncate` is\n  `outbound_comments.fit_preserving_marker` over the existing `_truncate_dc_comment_body`\n  at the `comment_max_chars()` ceiling — the composition Cloud's send path uses in\n  `acli_cli_ops.add_comment` (commit 6724e79e8f). A marker-less body goes straight to the\n  raw fit, so existing `sanitize_comment` behaviour on undecorated bodies stays\n  byte-identical (049e ceiling tests pass unchanged). Ceiling resolution is untouched.\n- **Keep the dedup key synchronized with what lands (the class commit 103729e90c fixed\n  for Cloud).** Re-derive `_DCSanitizer.fit_comment` via\n  `outbound_comments.fit_comment_as_sent` over the same raw fit — the marker-stripped\n  body the fitted send actually lands — mirroring Cloud's post-e339 `fit_comment`. Both\n  sides change in this one change. In-limit bodies return byte-identical.\n- **Cloud's dead `sanitize_comment` is REMOVED, not wired.** Cloud's live send fit is\n  `fit_preserving_marker(body, AdfCodec.fit_outbound)` (measures SERIALIZED ADF); the\n  dead method applies a plain 32,767-char cap that would cut the RECONCILER_MARKER if\n  ever wired — the false assurance the AC names. Remove `_JiraSanitizer.sanitize_comment`,\n  its delegate `jira_fields._sanitize_comment`, the `acli.py` facade re-export, and the\n  `FieldSanitizer.sanitize_comment` protocol member (nothing calls it through the port;\n  DC keeps its concrete, now-wired method — a Protocol permits extra members).\n\n## Scope\n\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py` — recompose `sanitize_comment`\n  (marker-preserving), re-derive `fit_comment` (as-sent), wire `add_comment`.\n- `adapters/jira/backend.py`, `adapters/jira/jira_fields.py`, `adapters/jira/acli.py`,\n  `_backend.py` — remove the dead Cloud `sanitize_comment` chain + protocol member.\n- `outbound_comments.py` — `fit_comment_as_sent` docstring: no longer Cloud-only.\n- Tests: NEW `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_send_path_comment_fit.py`; update\n  `test_dc_comment_ceiling_049e.py`'s convergence test to the as-sent contract; remove\n  the Cloud `sanitize_comment` characterization tests in\n  `test_backend_characterization.py`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- **RED (wiring):** build `JiraDataCenterBackend` over the REAL transport (`_links.py`\n  mixins) with a stubbed jira client recording the body it receives; send an\n  over-ceiling RECONCILER_MARKER-decorated body through `backend.add_comment`; assert\n  the wire body is `<= comment_max_chars()` and still ends with the marker. Fails\n  pre-fix, passes post-fix.\n- **RED (dedup-key):** for the same over-length body, `sanitizer.fit_comment(user_body)`\n  equals the marker-stripped wire body captured from the send path (the e339 class).\n- **Edges:** an in-limit decorated body passes through byte-identical; a `0` (unlimited)\n  ceiling passes an over-stock-length body through untouched.\n- Existing suites stay green: `test_dc_comment_ceiling_049e.py`,\n  `test_dc_outbound_comment_length_convergence.py`, `test_dc_backend_characterization.py`,\n  `test_backend_characterization.py`, `diffing/`, `mutate/`.\n- Verify: targeted `pytest -q` over the files above, then `make lint`, `make typecheck`,\n  `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The DC outbound send path fits comment bodies to the deployment-resolved ceiling —\n      checked: new send-path test asserts the transport-client-captured wire body\n      length is `<= comment_max_chars()`.\n- [x] The RECONCILER_MARKER survives the DC fit via the reused `fit_preserving_marker` —\n      checked: the same test asserts the captured wire body ends with the marker.\n- [x] The new send-path test is RED on pre-fix code — checked: run it against the\n      unmodified tree and observe the failure before committing the fix.\n- [x] `_DCSanitizer.fit_comment` equals the marker-stripped body the fitted send lands\n      (e339 dedup-key consistency) — checked: the new consistency test and the updated\n      049e convergence test pass.\n- [x] Cloud's `sanitize_comment` is removed (rationale in Approach) — checked:\n      `grep -rn \"def sanitize_comment\" src/rebar | grep -qv jira_datacenter | grep -qv\n      jira_family; test $? -ne 0` (only the DC implementation and the shared\n      `jira_family` helper remain).\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, the targeted pytest selection, and\n      `python 